## About this document
These are the terms on which TarragonHealth provides its services. They are Schedule C of our legal documents. The others are our Data Processing Consent and our Telehealth Consent.

## Acceptance of these terms
By ticking the box to accept and enrolling with TarragonHealth, you agree to these terms, our Data Processing Consent and our Telehealth Consent. If you do not agree, do not use the platform.

## Eligibility and accounts
You must be at least 18 years old to hold your own account. An adult may enrol a child under 18 as their dependant and manage the child's care, under our Guardian and dependant data terms. Each person, including a minor, has their own account and their own record. We do not offer a shared household or family account, or a discount for several people.

You may name a next of kin. A next of kin can be contacted in an emergency and, with your consent, can view your record but cannot edit it. An adult who wants help managing their own care can also set up an arrangement that lets another adult manage bookings on their behalf. Either person can end that arrangement at any time.

You are responsible for the accuracy of the information you provide, including anything you record for a dependant, and for keeping your login secure.

## What TarragonHealth is, and is not
TarragonHealth is a digital-first platform for long-term conditions, prevention and care coordination. We measure your readings, classify them against a clinical protocol, connect you with a doctor when something needs attention, and coordinate laboratories, pharmacies and specialist referrals on your behalf. We do not own or run any hospital, clinic, laboratory or screening facility. Every laboratory, pharmacy and specialist you use through the platform is an independent partner.

We are not an emergency service. See Emergencies below and our Telehealth Consent.

We are not an insurer. Nothing on the platform is capitation, claims cover or any other form of risk transfer. Where we bill an organisation for its members' access, that is a service fee, never a per-member premium.

## Individual and organisational access
You can join and pay for a plan yourself. An employer, HMO or other organisation may also pay for your Membership. If an organisation pays, you receive the same Membership as anyone else. The organisation only ever sees aggregate statistics about its whole covered group, never anything about you individually (see our Data Processing Consent). Your results, notes and messages stay between you and your care team. The organisation cannot ask us for them.

When an organisation pays, you have no payment relationship with TarragonHealth, and only the organisation that paid can claim the 21-day refund. Any refund goes back to that organisation. If the organisation claims a refund, we tell you, and your Member access ends at once, as it does for any approved refund. You keep your right to a make-good if we fail to deliver the service itself (see "Refunds, and if we do not deliver" below), and your records stay with you.

## The plans: Free, Membership and Membership Plus
There are three plans.

**Free.** The app, including health tracking, reminders, the screening calendar, education and guidance. Free does not include time with a doctor. See "If you are on the Free plan" below for what that means when a reading or symptom looks dangerous.

**Membership.** A year of care with your care team, on your phone. It includes:

- a video call with your care team every month, 12 in the year;
- written questions to your care team between calls; and
- prescriptions that your care team signs, for you to take to any pharmacy.

The yearly blood test is not included in Membership.

**Membership Plus.** Everything in Membership, plus a yearly blood test. Your results are uploaded to your account, and your care team talks them through with you.

Membership and Membership Plus are the same care. You get the same care team, the same monthly video call and the same urgent-care guidance. The only difference is the yearly blood test. What you pay buys scope, never a lower standard of care.

**How the monthly call works.** Each month your doctor offers you times and you choose one. The call is by video. If video does not work for you, it can be by audio only or by phone. "Every month" is the pace we plan for. It is not a promise that a call can never move by a few days. If we miss a month for a reason on our side, "Refunds, and if we do not deliver" below applies.

**The yearly blood test.** The yearly blood panel is a fixed set of tests. The list is shown on our pricing page. Membership Plus blood tests are collected in the state you choose when you buy, and that state stays fixed. If you later move somewhere we do not collect, you will need to come back to that state for your yearly tests. On any plan, including Free, you can ask for the yearly test request, take it to a laboratory and pay the laboratory directly. We do not collect blood on that route.

**Not included.**

- Medicines. Your care team signs a prescription and you take it to any pharmacy you choose and pay there.
- Tests, scans and hospital care beyond what is listed above. If your doctor advises more, we tell you roughly what it costs before you decide.
- Emergency care. See Emergencies below.
- The extras for Members described next.

## Extras for Members
Members can buy two extras. One is a second opinion from a doctor. The other is an extra online meeting with a doctor. Both are for Members only, so a person on the Free plan cannot buy them. The price of each is shown in the app before you confirm, and nothing is charged until you confirm.

You pay when you ask for an extra online meeting. A meeting is never automatic and depends on doctor availability. If no doctor accepts within 48 hours, or a doctor declines, or you do not choose one of the times offered within 24 hours, your payment is refunded in full.

## Price and payment
The price of each plan is shown on the screen where you pay, before you pay, together with what is included and the refund rule. It is also on your receipt. All prices are in naira. The same price applies whether you pay with a Nigerian payment method or an international card, and we do not run a separate foreign-currency price list. Payment is handled by Paystack. We do not see or store your full card details.

Your plan starts when we receive confirmation of payment from Paystack and runs for 12 months from that day.

**Moving up to Membership Plus.** You can move from Membership to Membership Plus at any time in the year. You pay only the difference, once, and your year does not change. Moving the other way can only happen when your year ends.

## No automatic renewal
Your plan does not renew by itself. Nothing is charged to your card again unless you choose to buy again. We aim to remind you 30, 14 and 7 days before your year ends, so that you can buy another year if you want to. If you do nothing, your plan ends on its end date. If we ever offer automatic renewal, it will be something you choose when you pay, and we will change these terms first.

## When your year ends
When your year ends naturally, you keep your Member access for 14 more days. During those 14 days you can still use your Member services, and you can buy a new year without a gap. After the 14 days your account returns to the Free plan. Your health record is kept and stays yours. You can always read and download it at no charge. Buying a plan again restores your Member access.

## Care Vouchers
When you pay for a health check or screening ahead of time, you receive a Care Voucher for that specific service. A voucher is an entitlement to the named service. It is not a store of money and not an account balance, and these terms apply to it.

**It is single-purpose.** A voucher can only be used for the service named on it. It cannot be applied to a different test, a different product, or a Membership.

**It is non-transferable.** A voucher belongs to the person it was issued to and cannot be sold, given away, or moved to another account. Neither you nor we can reassign it.

**It is never redeemable for cash.** There is no withdrawal, payout, or transfer route of any kind, and we will not create one. If a voucher is cancelled, any refund is made to the card or account that originally paid for it, never as cash and never as credit to somebody else.

**It is valid for 24 months** from the day it is fully paid for. We will tell you 30 days before it expires. If it does expire unused, contact us: we will normally extend it, and we would rather you got the care than lost the money.

**You can pay for it in instalments.** A voucher you are still paying for is reserved rather than active, and becomes usable once the full amount is paid. We do not expire a voucher you are still paying toward, and the 24 months only begins once it is fully paid.

**Someone else can buy one for you.** A family member or sponsor, including one living abroad, can buy a named service for you if you have linked them to your care. They will see that they bought it and later that it was used. They will not see your results or any other health information.

**Rewards are vouchers too.** Credit earned through referrals, prevention activities, or wellness points is issued as a discount voucher on these same terms. It has no cash value, was not bought with your money, and cannot be exchanged for money.

## Refunds, and if we do not deliver
**The 21-day refund.** You can ask for a refund of your Membership or Membership Plus within 21 days of buying it. The 21 days start at the time we receive confirmation of your payment and end at the same time of day, 21 days later. A request made before then is in time. If you ask in time, we refund the full price you paid. If you moved up from Membership to Membership Plus, the 21 days for that extra payment start on the day you paid it.

**After 21 days.** After 21 days, a plan is not refundable, except as set out under "If we do not deliver" below and except where the law requires a refund.

**What happens to your access.** When we approve a refund, your Member access ends straight away. You move to the Free plan, with no 14-day grace period. Your health record is kept and stays yours. The one exception is a refund of only the extra payment for moving up to Membership Plus. In that case you go back to Membership for the rest of your year, and you keep your Member access.

**How to ask.** Use the Request a refund option on your Membership page in the app, or write to legal@tarragonhealth.ng from the email address on your account. Tell us your name and the date you bought. Please add a few words on why you are asking. If an organisation paid for your Membership, only the organisation can ask, and we will not accept a refund request from the Member.

**How long it takes.** We reply within 5 working days. If we approve, we send the money back, through Paystack, to the card or bank account that paid, within 5 working days. Your bank then usually shows it within 3 to 10 working days after that. We do not charge you for a refund.

**If we do not deliver.** The 21-day limit does not take away any right you have if we fail to provide what you paid for. Suppose that, during your year, we cannot provide your yearly blood test (Membership Plus), or we repeatedly cannot provide your monthly calls, for a reason on our side. For example, no collection is available in the state you chose, or no doctor can offer you times. We will tell you, and offer you a choice:

1. a make-good, meaning we deliver the missing item by a new date we agree with you, and extend your Member access by the time it was missing if you ask; or
2. a refund of a fair share of the price for the part we did not deliver.

You choose. If an organisation paid for your Membership, you are entitled to the make-good for the service itself, and any refund goes to the organisation that paid.

This is how the share in option 2 is worked out. The yearly blood test is valued at the difference between the price of Membership Plus and the price of Membership. Each of the 12 monthly calls is valued at one twelfth of the price of Membership. We refund the value of the part we did not deliver, even if more than 21 days have passed.

If a missed item is your doing, it is not a reason on our side. For example, you booked a collection appointment and did not attend. We will still offer to rebook you once. Moving to a state where we do not collect is also not a reason on our side.

**Cancelling early.** You can stop using your plan at any time. After the first 21 days, we do not refund the unused part of a plan that you choose to give up, apart from the cases above.

**Other refunds.** A billing error, or a payment taken twice, is always refunded in full. A held payment for an extra online meeting that is never accepted is refunded as described above. A cancelled Care Voucher is refunded to the original payer as described under Care Vouchers.

**Your legal rights.** Nothing in this section removes any right you have under the law, including under the Federal Competition and Consumer Protection Act 2018.

## Your monitoring device
TarragonHealth does not sell, import, or supply blood-pressure cuffs, glucometers, or other monitoring devices. You buy your own device from any retailer of your choosing. Where your device uses a supported Bluetooth connection, our app can pair with it so a reading it takes can be logged to your record. Support for a specific device model is not a guarantee that the model will work with the app, and you should confirm compatibility before relying on it.

## Fees and price changes
We may change our prices. A price change never affects a purchase you have already made. It only applies to purchases made after the change takes effect, and we show you the price before you pay.

## Referral rewards
If you refer someone who joins TarragonHealth using your referral link or code, both of you may receive a reward voucher once they complete their first paid action on the platform. A reward voucher is a discount toward care on the terms set out under Care Vouchers above: it has no cash value and cannot be exchanged for money. Reward amounts and terms may change. We tell you the current amount before you share your link.

## Emergencies
TarragonHealth is not an emergency service. If you think you or someone with you is having an emergency, do not wait for the app, a message or a call from us. Call the emergency number for your area or go to the nearest hospital. Ask someone to go with you if you can.

## If you are on the Free plan
The Free plan does not include time with a doctor. This is what that means in practice.

If you record a reading or a symptom that looks dangerous, the app shows you straight away what to do: seek emergency care or go to the nearest hospital. For the most serious readings it also tells you plainly that no doctor has been alerted. Whatever the app shows you, no doctor is alerted about a reading or symptom logged on the Free plan. If you have named an emergency contact, we let them know. The app also asks you to check the reading again shortly afterwards, and checks in later to ask whether you were able to get care. Your answers stay in your own record and are not sent to a doctor.

An abnormal screening result, or a critical laboratory result, that reaches us is sent to a doctor on every plan.

On Membership and Membership Plus, a dangerous reading is seen by our care team as part of your care. You can join at any time. Please do not rely on the Free plan, or on the app, to watch your readings for you. If you feel unwell, get care.

## Records
We keep your health record while you use TarragonHealth and afterwards, including after a plan ends, after a refund and when you return to the Free plan, for the periods set out in our Data Processing Consent and as the law requires. You can read and download your record at any time.

You can withdraw any optional consent at any time, as easily as you gave it, as set out in the Data Processing Consent. The consents that your care depends on cannot be withdrawn while you keep your account. To end them, you ask us to close your account. If you withdraw an optional consent, some parts of the service that need your data may no longer be possible, and we will tell you which.

## Complaints
If something is wrong, write to legal@tarragonhealth.ng. We will acknowledge your message within 2 working days and give you an answer within 10 working days. If you are not happy with our answer, you may complain to the Federal Competition and Consumer Protection Commission (FCCPC) about the service or charges, to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission (NDPC) about your data, and to the Medical and Dental Council of Nigeria (MDCN) about the conduct of a doctor. You may also go to court.

## Acceptable use
You agree to provide accurate information, not to impersonate another person or misrepresent your relationship to a dependant or adult you manage, not to misuse the platform to harass our staff or other users, and not to attempt to bypass the platform's security or access controls.

## Intellectual property
The TarragonHealth name, brand, and the software and content that make up the platform belong to us or our licensors. We grant you a personal, non-transferable licence to use the platform for your own care or the care of a dependant or adult you manage. You may not copy, resell, or build a competing service from our platform or content.

## Third-party services
The platform links to and integrates with services we do not control, including Paystack, our video-call provider, and our partner laboratories, pharmacies and specialists. Your use of those services is subject to their own terms, and we are not responsible for their acts, omissions, or availability.

## Disclaimers and liability
The platform and the services are provided with reasonable care and skill. Remote care has limits, as explained in our Telehealth Consent: a doctor cannot examine you in person, and advice is based on what you tell us and what we can measure.

Nothing in these terms excludes or limits our liability for death or personal injury caused by our negligence, for fraud, or for anything else that the law does not allow us to exclude or limit. Any other limit on our liability applies only to the extent the law allows, and we will not rely on it where it would be unfair to you.

## Termination
We may suspend or terminate your account if you breach these terms, do not pay a fee that is due, or engage in conduct that puts our staff, other users, or the platform at risk. If we end your Membership because of your breach, we will tell you why. If we end it and you did nothing wrong, we refund the unused part of the price, valued in the same way as under "If we do not deliver" above.

## Changes to these terms
We may update these terms as the platform changes. We will show you the current version and ask you to accept it again if a material change affects your rights or obligations. A change never reduces what you have already paid for.

## Governing law and disputes
These terms are governed by the laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria. You may bring a dispute in the courts of Nigeria. Nothing in this section limits any right you have under the Federal Competition and Consumer Protection Act 2018 to complain to the FCCPC, or your right to complain to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission under our Data Processing Consent.

## Contact
Questions about these terms: legal@tarragonhealth.ng.
$tos_body$;
  v_tele_body text := $tele_body$
## About this document
This is TarragonHealth's Telehealth Consent, Schedule B of our legal documents. It sits alongside our Terms of Service and our Data Processing Consent.

## What this consent covers
This is your consent to receive clinical monitoring, classification and review from TarragonHealth remotely, and to be contacted by phone, message or in the app as part of that care. It is separate from, and in addition to, our Data Processing Consent and our Terms of Service.

Your plan decides how much of this involves a doctor. On Membership and Membership Plus, a doctor reviews your readings and results as part of your care. On the Free plan, the app checks your readings against the same rules and tells you what to do, but no doctor reviews them. The Terms of Service explain the plans.

## Your care team
Your care is provided by doctors registered with the Medical and Dental Council of Nigeria (MDCN). Their registration is verified before they can see patients and checked continuously afterwards. A doctor whose registration or indemnity cover lapses is automatically suspended from seeing patients overnight, with no manual step needed. Our doctors review readings under clinical protocols, start and adjust medications, and refer you on when needed. Care is shared across a team, so you may speak to different doctors at different times, and each one can see your record. Our Chief Medical Officer oversees the care team and signs the clinical protocols that everyone works under.

Non-clinical coordinators may also be involved in your care. They follow up if we have not heard from you, and they help with bookings and other practical matters. They can see your progress record, but they cannot read your clinical notes, interpret a result, adjust your medication or give clinical advice. Anything clinical is always handled by a doctor.

Every clinical note you can read shows the treating doctor's name and MDCN number.

## How your results are classified and how we respond
Every reading you log is classified automatically against a clinical protocol suited to its type. Even a normal reading gets a record, so nothing is silently skipped. Separately, an AI model may draft a plain-language summary of your record to help your doctor prepare for your case. It never classifies a result itself, never diagnoses and never closes a case. A summary is always labelled as AI-drafted until a doctor has actually reviewed it.

How quickly we respond depends on how a finding is classified. A routine screening result and a dangerous blood pressure reading carry different urgency, so there is no single flat response time. For Members, as a general guide:

- Routine findings are usually reviewed within days, as part of a batch.
- Findings that need attention but are not urgent are usually reviewed by a doctor within 3 days.
- Urgent findings usually get a phone or video call within hours, not a message alone.
- Emergency findings get immediate contact. If we cannot reach you, we document an attempt to reach your emergency contact.

A finding classified as an emergency cannot be closed on a written note alone. Your doctor must first have a real, live phone or video conversation with you before the case can be marked resolved.

These are standards we hold ourselves to. They are not a guarantee of a particular outcome in every case. How quickly we can reach you also depends on you being reachable.

On the Free plan, no doctor reviews a reading you log, so these times do not apply to readings. They do apply to two things on every plan: an abnormal screening result, and a critical laboratory result. Both are sent to a doctor whichever plan you are on. For an abnormal screening result, we aim to contact you within 24 hours, and within 12 hours if the result is critical.

## How we communicate with you
Different channels carry different kinds of information, on purpose.

- **The app is your record.** Your ongoing conversation with your care team, your results, your care plan and your consent history live here. The in-app conversation is the main channel for anything clinical.
- **A phone or video call is how clinical judgement is delivered.** If something in your results needs discussing, a doctor calls you by phone or video, and a note of the call is added to your record.
- **Two-way conversation with your care team happens in the app only.** Send a message any time. A real person on your care team reads it and replies there. No automated system turns what you send into an action on the platform.
- **Push notifications and in-app alerts** tell you that something is waiting for you, such as a reminder, a new message or a result to read. The detail is in the app.
- **Email** carries receipts, reminders and copies of your consent records. It does not carry your results or clinical advice.
- **Text messages (SMS)** are used only for phone verification codes. Care conversations happen in the app and by phone or video.

## What remote monitoring can and cannot do
Remote monitoring lets your care team review your readings and respond between visits, without you needing to travel for every check. It has real limits. Your doctor cannot examine you in person, and their assessment rests on the readings and information you provide. If something needs an in-person assessment, your care team will tell you and refer you appropriately, including, where relevant, to one of our partner laboratories, pharmacies or specialists.

## Emergency care
TarragonHealth does not provide emergency care. If you think you or someone with you is having a medical emergency, do not wait for the app, a message or a call from us. Call the emergency number for your area or go to the nearest hospital straight away. Ask someone to go with you if you can. No part of this platform is designed to be used in an emergency.

If you are on the Free plan, no doctor is alerted when you record a reading or symptom that looks dangerous. The app shows you what to do straight away, which is to seek emergency care or go to the nearest hospital. For the most serious readings it also tells you plainly that no doctor was alerted. Whatever the app shows you, no doctor is alerted about a reading or symptom logged on the Free plan. If you are a Member, a dangerous reading is seen by our care team as part of your care. That is still not an emergency service. In an emergency, go to the nearest hospital first.

## Confidentiality
Your clinical information is kept confidential. It is shared with your care team on a need-to-know basis. Outside the care team it is shared only with your specific consent, including a family member or sponsor you have separately agreed to give view access to, where the law requires disclosure, or where there is a serious threat to your life, health or public health. If an organisation pays for your Membership, it sees only aggregate figures about its whole covered group and never your individual results. See our Data Processing Consent for how we handle your data more broadly.

## Your right to information and to take part in your care
Every message and note tells you who is speaking to you, with their MDCN number where relevant. You can see every clinical action taken on your record, in plain language, at any time.

## Your right to consent, and to refuse
You can decline a specific recommendation. Declining does not end your access to the rest of the platform, unless what you are declining is safety-critical. In that case we will tell you clearly why.

## Withdrawing this consent
This consent is needed for the care we provide, so we cannot keep your account open without it. If you no longer agree, ask us to close your account and we will do so. Closing your account ends remote clinical review from that point on. It does not delete your existing health record, which we keep as set out in our Data Processing Consent. Declining a single recommendation, as described above, is different and does not need you to close your account.

## Contact
Questions about your care or this consent: support@tarragonhealth.ng.
$tele_body$;
  v_dp_body text := $dp_body$
## About this document
This is TarragonHealth's Data Processing Consent, Schedule A of our legal documents. It sits alongside our Terms of Service and our Telehealth Consent.

## Who we are
Tarragon Health Ltd (RC 9702108) ("TarragonHealth", "we", "us") operates a digital-first chronic disease, preventive health, and care-coordination platform in Nigeria, connecting patients with doctors, labs, pharmacies, specialists, employers, and HMOs. We are the data controller for the personal data described in this notice.

Our Data Protection Officer can be reached at privacy@tarragonhealth.ng. Tarragon Health Ltd is registered with the Nigeria Data Protection Commission (NDPC) as a data controller and processor of major importance.

If you have questions about this notice or how we handle your data, contact us at privacy@tarragonhealth.ng. That address reaches our Data Protection Officer.

## What personal data we collect
We collect the information you give us directly, the information your care team records about you, and the information generated by using the platform.

• Identity and contact details: name, date of birth, sex, phone number, email, state and local government area of residence.

• Emergency contact: the name and phone number of a next of kin, used to reach someone on your behalf in an emergency, or, with your consent, to let them view (not edit) your record.

• Health and clinical information: vitals readings (blood pressure, glucose, weight, and others); the device you use to take them; symptoms and messages you share with your care team; medications; screening and lab results; vaccination records; and clinical notes written by your doctor.

• Payment and voucher information: service purchase, Care Voucher, and order history, and payment references from Paystack. We do not store your full card number. Where someone buys you a Care Voucher, we record the purchase and the funding relationship between you.

• Device information: where you use a Bluetooth-paired reading device, its make, model, and serial number.

• Usage information: app and website activity, for security, fraud prevention, and service improvement.

## Sensitive personal data
Most of what we hold about you (your readings, symptoms, diagnoses, medications, and results) is health information, which the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 classifies as sensitive personal data. We apply extra safeguards to this category of data: it is only visible to your care team and to you, access is logged, and every clinical action taken on your record is written to a record you can read yourself.

## Why we process your data, and the specific consents we ask for
We rely on more than one lawful basis, depending on the purpose.

• Delivery of your care: processing your readings, symptoms, and clinical information to classify your results, alert your care team, and maintain your record is necessary for the provision of healthcare by a licensed clinician under a duty of confidentiality.

• Specific, scoped consent: for anything beyond your direct care, we ask for a specific consent, tracked individually:

• Escalation contact: your consent for us to message or call you if we do not hear from you when we should. This is asked at enrolment and is required to activate your account.

• Clinical share: your consent to share your clinical information with a specific named recipient, for example a specialist you are referred to.

• Family/sponsor access: a family member, next of kin, or sponsor funding your care may, with your separate consent, view your record or manage bookings on your behalf. Funding your care never grants this access automatically; it is a separate, two-sided request either of you can initiate and either of you can decline.

• Institution aggregate: if you are enrolled through an employer or HMO programme, your data contributes to that organisation's aggregate statistics in de-identified form regardless of this consent, because the organisation never sees anything about you individually. See "Who we share your data with" below.

• Research, anonymised: your optional consent for your anonymised data to be used in research. This is off by default. If you consent and later withdraw, we stop including you in future research exports, but we cannot recall an export already delivered before you withdrew.

• Legal obligation: we process certain data, for example payment and tax records, to meet our obligations under Nigerian law.

Some consents are required to hold an account, because our care cannot work without them: this notice, our Terms of Service, our Telehealth Consent and the escalation contact consent. You cannot withdraw a required consent and keep your account. To end one, ask us to close your account (see "Deleting your account" below). Every other consent is optional, and you can withdraw it at any time, as easily as you gave it.

## Where your data is stored, and international transfer
Your data is stored in a Postgres database operated by our infrastructure provider, Supabase, in the AWS eu-west-1 region (Ireland). We use this region because our provider does not currently offer a data centre in Nigeria or elsewhere in Africa; eu-west-1 is the nearest available region.

This means your personal data, including sensitive health information, leaves Nigeria as a routine part of how the platform runs, not as an occasional or optional event. Nigerian law requires a specific lawful mechanism before personal data is transferred outside Nigeria. This is the highest-priority open item in our own legal review.

Separately, a summarising step assisting your doctor's own review (see "Automated processing" below) sends a limited, structured extract of your record (never your free-text notes) to a second processor, Anthropic, whose infrastructure is also outside Nigeria.

We have not yet finalised the lawful mechanism for either of these two transfers. This section tells you that both transfers happen. It does not say that a specific legal mechanism is in place for either.

## Automated processing
Every reading you log is automatically classified against a clinical protocol appropriate to its type; this always happens, even for a normal reading, so nothing is silently skipped. Separately, an AI model may draft a plain-language summary of your record for your doctor to review before they act on your case; it never diagnoses, never closes a case, never prescribes, and every summary is labelled as AI-drafted and not yet reviewed until a doctor has actually looked at it.

When you tap "Help me understand this" on a reading or risk signal, the same kind of AI tool drafts a short, plain-language explanation: never a diagnosis, just a way to understand the number in front of you. As with the doctor-facing summary, this explanation is only ever a draft: it does not replace your doctor's own review, and a real doctor always makes the actual decision about your care.

A result classified urgent or emergency can only be closed by your doctor after they have spoken with you directly by phone or video; it cannot be closed from a written note alone. You may ask us for an explanation of any automated assessment shown to you.

## Who we share your data with
We share your data only as needed to provide your care and run the platform.

• Your care team: the doctors and coordinators involved in your care.

• A specific person or organisation you have separately consented to share with. See "Clinical share" and "Family/sponsor access" above.

• Your employer or HMO, where you are enrolled through their programme, only as aggregate statistics with no individual identified; any figure drawn from too few people is withheld rather than shown. We tell every patient plainly: TarragonHealth does not share individual health records with your employer.

• Our payment processor, Paystack, to process a payment you have initiated, and (for a limited, structured extract only) Anthropic, to draft a doctor-facing summary. See "Automated processing" above.

• Regulators, courts, or other authorities, where we are legally required to disclose information.

• Anonymised research exports, only for patients who have separately opted in (see "Research, anonymised" above), built so no individual can be re-identified from the output.

We do not sell your personal data.

## How long we keep your data
We keep your data for as long as you have an active enrolment, and for a further period after that to meet our clinical record-keeping and legal obligations.

We are finalising a retention schedule with exact periods for each kind of data. Until it is published, we handle each deletion request one at a time, applying the most careful retention period that could apply.

## Your rights
Under Nigerian data protection law, you have the right to:

• Access the personal data we hold about you, and export it yourself at any time; this works from your first login and is never conditional on your subscription or payment being up to date.

• Ask us to correct inaccurate or incomplete data.

• Ask us to erase your data, subject to our clinical and legal retention obligations.

• Object to, or ask us to restrict, certain processing.

• Withdraw an optional consent at any time. A required consent ends only when you close your account.

• Lodge a complaint with the Nigeria Data Protection Commission (ndpc.gov.ng), or with us directly at privacy@tarragonhealth.ng.

## Deleting your account
You can ask us to delete your TarragonHealth account and the personal data we hold about you at any time. There are three ways to do it:

• In the app: open More, then Privacy & your data, and tap "Request deletion of your data".

• On the web: sign in at app.tarragonhealth.ng, open Privacy & your data, and choose "Request deletion of your data".

• By email: write to privacy@tarragonhealth.ng from the email address on your account. We will confirm it is really you before acting on the request.

What happens next: a member of our team reviews every request. You can see its status on the same Privacy & your data page. Some clinical records must be kept for a minimum period under Nigerian healthcare regulation and the retention rules described above; if that applies to part of your record, we will tell you exactly what can and cannot be deleted before we complete the request. Everything that is not subject to a retention obligation, including your account, sign-in, contact details, paired-device details, and any data synced from a connected device or health app, is deleted when the request is completed. Once completed, the deletion cannot be undone.

Deleting your account never depends on a payment being up to date, and you do not need to give a reason.

## Security
We restrict access to your data to the staff who need it for your care, encrypt data in transit and at rest, and keep an immutable log of every access to and change of your clinical record. No system is completely secure, and we will tell you and, where the law requires it, the NDPC, if we become aware of a breach affecting your personal data.

## Guardian and dependant data
If you enrol a child under 18 as your dependant, you are their guardian for the purposes of this notice: you confirm you have the legal authority to consent to their information being processed, and you are responsible for the accuracy of what you record on their behalf. Each person, including a minor, has their own individually-structured record; we do not offer a shared or household account.


## Changes to this notice
We may update this notice as the platform changes. We will show you the current version and ask you to accept it again if a material change affects how your data is used.

## Contact and complaints
Email privacy@tarragonhealth.ng with any question, request, or complaint about how we handle your data. You may also complain directly to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission.
$dp_body$;
  v_all text;
  v_other_before text;
  v_other_after text;
begin
  if v_version like 'SET-AT-PUBLISH%' then
    raise exception 'version is still the placeholder; the owner has not signed';
  end if;

  -- strict: raises if there is no current row, or more than one.
  select title into strict v_terms_title
    from public.consent_versions
   where consent_type = 'terms_of_service' and is_current;
  select title into strict v_tele_title
    from public.consent_versions
   where consent_type = 'telehealth' and is_current;
  select title into strict v_dp_title
    from public.consent_versions
   where consent_type = 'data_processing' and is_current;
  v_all := v_terms_body || v_tele_body || v_dp_body;

  if exists (select 1 from public.consent_versions
              where consent_type in ('terms_of_service', 'telehealth', 'data_processing')
                and version = v_version) then
    raise exception 'version % already exists for a consent being published', v_version;
  end if;

  -- Guards: refuse to publish a draft.
  if position('[' in v_all) > 0 then
    raise exception 'unresolved square-bracket placeholder in a consent body';
  end if;
  if v_all like '%' || chr(8212) || '%' or v_all like '%' || chr(8211) || '%' then
    raise exception 'em dash or en dash in a consent body';
  end if;
  if v_all ~* '(whatsapp|stripe|health wallet|platform credit)' then
    raise exception 'retired channel, provider or product named in a consent body';
  end if;
  if v_terms_body !~ '21-day refund' then
    raise exception 'terms body is missing the 21-day refund';
  end if;

  select md5(coalesce(string_agg(id::text, ',' order by id), ''))
    into v_other_before
    from public.consent_versions
   where is_current and consent_type not in ('terms_of_service', 'telehealth', 'data_processing');

  update public.consent_versions
     set is_current = false
   where consent_type in ('terms_of_service', 'telehealth', 'data_processing') and is_current;

  insert into public.consent_versions (consent_type, version, title, body, is_current)
  values ('terms_of_service', v_version, v_terms_title, v_terms_body, true),
         ('telehealth', v_version, v_tele_title, v_tele_body, true),
         ('data_processing', v_version, v_dp_title, v_dp_body, true);

  -- Assertions: provable, not hopeful.
  if (select count(*) from public.consent_versions
       where consent_type = 'terms_of_service' and is_current) <> 1 then
    raise exception 'exactly one terms_of_service version must be current';
  end if;
  if (select count(*) from public.consent_versions
       where consent_type = 'telehealth' and is_current) <> 1 then
    raise exception 'exactly one telehealth version must be current';
  end if;
  if not exists (select 1 from public.consent_versions
                  where consent_type = 'terms_of_service' and is_current
                    and version = v_version
                    and body like '%Membership Plus%'
                    and body like '%No automatic renewal%'
                    and body like '%no doctor has been alerted%') then
    raise exception 'new terms body is missing expected content';
  end if;
  if (select count(*) from public.consent_versions
       where consent_type = 'data_processing' and is_current) <> 1 then
    raise exception 'exactly one data_processing version must be current';
  end if;
  if not exists (select 1 from public.consent_versions
                  where consent_type = 'data_processing' and is_current
                    and version = v_version
                    and body like '%ndpc.gov.ng%'
                    and body like '%close your account%') then
    raise exception 'new data_processing body is missing expected content';
  end if;
  if not exists (select 1 from public.consent_versions
                  where consent_type = 'telehealth' and is_current
                    and version = v_version
                    and body like '%Free plan%') then
    raise exception 'new telehealth body is missing expected content';
  end if;

  select md5(coalesce(string_agg(id::text, ',' order by id), ''))
    into v_other_after
    from public.consent_versions
   where is_current and consent_type not in ('terms_of_service', 'telehealth', 'data_processing');
  if v_other_before is distinct from v_other_after then
    raise exception 'the other consent types were disturbed';
  end if;
end $$;
